                <pb facs="0853" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/249: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-29T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1922—3
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>160. Department’s No. 92 of April 20, 4 p.m.<anchor n="69" xml:id="d505-f1"/></p>
                <p>The Italian Government having acquiesced this government is instructing its
                    representatives at London, Paris, Tokyo, Rome, Brussels, The Hague and Lisbon,
                    to approach the Governments to which they are respectively accredited with the
                    request that they each now indicate their formal approval of the resolution in
                    amended form (see page 737 of Senate Document 126<anchor n="70" xml:id="d505-f2"
                    />) which was offered during the Conference on Limitation of Armaments at
                    Washington. You will inform those of your colleagues who represent powers which
                    participated in the Conference of this action on the part of this
                    Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
